  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that Santander obtained rights in the debt but the debt is still owed or due to Sam's Cars."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondent says the provision at issue applies to a bank holding debts as collateral, not to a debt collector."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Santander",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Santander contends that \u201cowed\u201d and \u201cdue\u201d have subtly different meanings; a debt can be owed but not yet due."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Santander",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Santander, santander states the key question is whether it was a debt collector at the time of the alleged violation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Santander",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Santander argues it may fall within the assignee exclusion, which applies to a person who receives a debt assignment solely to facilitate collection for another."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Santander",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Santander, santander notes its servicing activity in 2012 was much less than today, indicating a different business context at the time of the alleged violations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Counsel",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 54,
              "start": 54
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Counsel, counsel alleges that the petitioner's proposed solution to subsection (F)(iv) does not work and lacks any coherent sense."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 54,
              "start": 54
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, respondent alleges that a third\u2011party debt collector can evade the statutes if hired before a debt goes into default, even once it is delinquent."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-188cd69e39a2-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 55,
              "start": 55
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts noted that the case has been submitted to the Court."
      }
    ],
